WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.087
Module 2 covers edge interception,
DNS identity and DNSSEC.

2
00:00:05.087 --> 00:00:08.346
Every policy control assumes
the query reaches it,

3
00:00:08.346 --> 00:00:12.613
so we'll look at three ordinary ways
it doesn't, none of which reports.

4
00:00:12.613 --> 00:00:15.578
Then why a perfectly valid certificate can

5
00:00:15.578 --> 00:00:18.700
still fail because of
DNS, and finally DNSSEC.
